      "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #52613.\n\nWith MiniMax-M3 (`stream: true` + tools), generation halts after the reasoning block closes — empty delta with `finish_reason: stop`, no tool call produced. Non-streaming works fine.\n\n**Root cause:** MiniMax-M3 sometimes elides (skips) the opening tag for a parameter, producing `value]<]minimax[>[</param_name>` instead of `]<]minimax[>[<param_name>value]<]minimax[>[</param_name>`. The parser's `_parse_invoke_params()` expects `ELEMENT_START` at the current position; when it's missing, parsing stops — losing all remaining parameters.\n\n**Fix** (`vllm/parser/minimax_m3.py`): Add `_recover_untagged_param()` that recovers elided-opener parameters by extracting the name from the closing tag. Includes a guard: if a well-formed opening tag appears before the closing tag, recovery is skipped (the text is junk before a valid element, not an elided opener).\n\n## Test Results\n\n**Unit tests (CPU):** 10/10 custom tests + 17/17 existing tests (`test_minimax_m3.py`) passed.\n\n**GPU E2E:** Not testable locally — MiniMax-M3 is a 456B MoE model. The fix is verified via comprehensive unit tests covering elided tag recovery, well-formed parsing, the regression guard, and edge cases.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- [x] Custom unit tests for elided tag recovery and the regression guard\n- [x] Existing `test_minimax_m3.py` tests pass (17/17)\n- [x] Well-formed output parsed identically (recovery branch only triggers on missing opener)\n\n## Notes\n\n- The recovery only activates when text doesn't start with `ELEMENT_START` — well-formed output takes the existing code path.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
